*Unsolicited Application at MB Shipbrokers, R&D Student Assistant*


Dear MB Shipbrokers,

My name is Mathias and I am currently pursuing a MSc in Mathematical Modelling and Computational Science at the Technical University of Denmark (DTU). I am writing to express my interest in the R&D Student Assistant position at MB Shipbrokers. With a strong background in applied mathematics, software development, and a proactive approach to problem-solving. I am currently working on time series analysis, machine learning and algorithms. Having previously worked on ships as a "Matros" I have a sincere interest in the maritime industry and wish to apply my knowlegde and know how in this field.

Working in a start-up (VetAlign) and a small consultancy (NORDIC MARINE PARTNER) learns you a lot about how take responsibility and critically find the most crucial tasks at hand, but I have in both occasions been missing the opportunity to learn from the best of the best in the industry. Therefore, I am excited by the prospect of learning from industry-leading experts, who are good at explaining complex data-driven decisions to colleagues outside R&D.

My entrepreneurial experience as a Co-founder of VetAlign has honed my ability to build complex systems from the ground up. I successfully developed a fully functional SaaS product using *C\# and NextJS*, which gave me deep insight into building reliable software architectures. Additionally, my technical toolkit includes experience with *F\#, Java, and Typescript*, as well as specialized knowledge in *Forecasting, Time Series Analysis, and Machine Learning* which was mainly done in Python. I thrive in environments where I can do sparring with colleagues to technical challenges and solve problems with a proactive, initiative-driven approach.


